# General LLM Anti-Patterns (continued)

Companion to `general-llm-anti-patterns.mdc`. Section numbers preserved.

## Category 10: Modern LLM Capability Anti-Patterns

### 10.1 Reasoning Mode Misuse (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** Don't use reasoning modes for simple tasks that don't require complex analysis.

❌ Bad: Using reasoning mode for trivial operations, extended reasoning for straightforward code, verbose reasoning for simple tasks
✅ Good: Use reasoning modes only for complex multi-step tasks, instant mode for simple operations, brief reasoning for straightforward code
⚠️ Why: Wastes tokens, adds latency, unnecessary for simple tasks, slows down simple operations
🔧 Fix: Use reasoning modes only when truly needed; use instant mode for simple tasks; match mode to task complexity

**Detect:** Reasoning mode for simple operations, extended reasoning for straightforward code, verbose reasoning for trivial tasks, unnecessary reasoning mode usage

---

### 10.2 Long Context Waste (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** Don't use @codebase for single-file changes. Use @filename for targeted context.

❌ Bad: `@codebase` for single-file changes, loading entire repository for localized edits, no context management
✅ Good: `@filename` for targeted changes, load only necessary files, manage context size actively
⚠️ Why: Wastes tokens, reduces coherence, slows processing, unnecessary context loading
🔧 Fix: Use @filename for targeted changes; load only necessary files; manage context size actively
📍 See: `cursor-integration.mdc` section 1.2

**Detect:** @codebase for single-file changes, entire repo loading for localized edits, no context size management, excessive context usage

---

### 10.3 Multimodal Misuse (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** Don't request image analysis for text-only tasks. Use visual aids only for UI/design work.

❌ Bad: Requesting image analysis for text-only tasks, including screenshots when code inspection would suffice, visual analysis for non-visual problems
✅ Good: Use visual aids only for UI/design work, text descriptions for code issues, images for visual problems only
⚠️ Why: Wastes tokens, adds latency, unnecessary processing, slows down text-only tasks
🔧 Fix: Use images only for visual problems; use text for code issues; match input type to task
📍 See: `general-llm-anti-patterns-07-09.mdc` section 9.2 (Verbose Text-Only Prompts)

**Detect:** Image analysis for text-only tasks, screenshots for code inspection, visual analysis for non-visual problems, multimodal input when text suffices

---

### 10.4 Structured Output Overuse (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** Don't force structured output when plain text is clearer.

❌ Bad: JSON schemas for simple responses, structured output for straightforward text, forcing structure when text suffices
✅ Good: Use structured output only for machine-readable data, plain text for simple responses, match format to use case
⚠️ Why: Adds complexity, wastes tokens, unnecessary structure, makes simple responses harder
🔧 Fix: Use structured output only when needed; use plain text for simple responses; match format to use case

**Detect:** JSON schemas for simple responses, structured output for straightforward text, forcing structure when text suffices, unnecessary structured formats

---

### 10.5 Tool Use Anti-Patterns (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** Don't over-call tools or invent tool parameters. Batch operations when possible.

❌ Bad: Over-calling tools for simple operations, not batching tool calls, inventing tool parameters, single tool call per item in loop
✅ Good: Batch tool calls when possible, verify tool parameters, use tools efficiently, combine related operations
⚠️ Why: Adds latency, wastes tokens, inefficient processing, slower execution
🔧 Fix: Batch tool calls when possible; verify tool parameters; use tools efficiently; combine related operations

**Detect:** Over-calling tools, not batching tool calls, inventing tool parameters, single tool call per item, inefficient tool usage

---

### 10.6 Extended Reasoning Anti-Patterns (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** Don't use extended reasoning for simple operations.

❌ Bad: Extended reasoning for simple operations, excessive reasoning traces for straightforward code, long reasoning for trivial tasks
✅ Good: Extended reasoning only for complex multi-step tasks, brief reasoning for simple operations, reasoning checkpoints for long tasks
⚠️ Why: Wastes compute time, adds latency, unnecessary for simple operations, slows down simple tasks
🔧 Fix: Use extended reasoning only for complex tasks; use brief reasoning for simple operations; add checkpoints for long tasks

**Detect:** Extended reasoning for simple operations, excessive traces for straightforward code, long reasoning for trivial tasks, unnecessary extended reasoning

---

### 10.7 Large Context Window Misuse (CRIT)

**CRITICAL:** Don't load entire codebase when targeted files suffice, even with large context capacity.

❌ Bad: Loading entire codebase for single-file changes, using @codebase for localized edits, no context window management
✅ Good: Use @filename for targeted changes, manage context window size, only load necessary files
⚠️ Why: Reduces coherence even with large capacity, slows processing, wastes tokens, unnecessary context loading
🔧 Fix: Use targeted file loading; manage context size actively; only load necessary files for task
📍 See: `cursor-integration.mdc` section 1.2, `general-llm-anti-patterns-07-09.mdc` section 7.2a

**Detect:** @codebase for single-file changes, entire repo loading unnecessarily, no context size management, context window exhaustion

